msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Rotate Image</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can rotate the image. The top part of the dialog shows "
"the result of the rotation in the form of a change in dimension (if any). "
"Under <guilabel>Direction</guilabel> you can choose between rotating "
"clockwise and counter-clockwise. Under <guilabel>Angle</guilabel>, you can "
"set the amount of rotation. 90, 180 and 270 degrees can be selected using "
"the respective option button, other amounts need to be specified with the "
"<guilabel>Custom</guilabel> spin box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Separate Image</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Separate Image</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Separate Image</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Separate Image</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can separate (part of) your image. Every color "
"component (channel) will be put into a separate layer or image. At the top "
"of the dialog, the current color model is shown. Below that, a couple of "
"options can be set."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Source</guilabel>, you can choose what part of the image to "
"separate. The two options are <guilabel>Current layer</guilabel>, which "
"(obviously) only uses the currently selected layer and <guilabel>Flatten all "
"layers before separation</guilabel>, which uses the entire image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Output</guilabel>, you can choose where the result of the "
"separation should be written to: either to a couple of layers, or to a "
"couple of images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Alpha Options</guilabel>, you can choose what should be done "
"with the alpha channel of the selected layer(s). It can be copied to each "
"new channel, be discarded, or separated on its own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The two options at the bottom of the dialog, finally, determine whether the "
"source should be downscaled to 8 bit colors (if it contains more), and "
"whether the output should be in color (default is to separate the channels "
"to grayscale values)."
msgstr ""

