#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog, similar to the <link linkend=\"commands-dialogs-image-"
"rotateimage\"><guilabel>Rotate Image</guilabel> dialog</link>, allows you to "
"rotate the current layer. You can choose the direction in which to rotate "
"and the amount to rotate the layer by."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Shear Layer</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Shear Layer</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Shear Layer</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Shear Layer</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog works the same as the <link linkend=\"commands-dialogs-image-"
"shearimage\"><guilabel>Shear Image</guilabel> dialog</link>, except that it "
"operates on the current layer instead of on the entire image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dialogs for working with filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All filter dialogs consist of a filter-specific part, at the left, and a "
"generic part, at the right. The generic part contains a preview window, "
"which you can configure using the controls below it. Choose "
"<guilabel>Preview</guilabel> or <guilabel>Original</guilabel> depending on "
"whether you want the preview window to show the preview of the filter effect "
"or the original image. The four buttons at the bottom right allow you to "
"zoom in and zoom out, set the zooming factor to 100% (this shows the image "
"at its original size), and refresh the preview, respectively. Furthermore, "
"the option <guilabel>Autoupdate</guilabel> determines if the preview window "
"is updated automatically. If you uncheck this checkbox, you will have to "
"refresh the preview yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Blur</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Blur</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Blur</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Blur</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog allows you to customize the way your image is blurred. The "
"<guilabel>Half-width</guilabel> and <guilabel>Half-height</guilabel> "
"spinboxes determine the size of the areas of your image that are "
"consecutively blurred. With the <guilabel>Strength</guilabel> spinbox you "
"can set the strength with which the blurring should be applied, and with the "
"<guilabel>Angle</guilabel> spinbox you can add a rotation to the area. The "
"<guilabel>Shape</guilabel> setting, finally, allows you to choose between "
"circular and rectangular areas"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Brightness / Contrast</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Brightness / Contrast</guilabel> dialog</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Brightness / Contrast</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Brightness / Contrast</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can customize the brightness and contrast of your "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The curve diagram has a histogram-like background that shows you the "
"abundance of various brightness levels. The curve itself (initially a "
"diagonal line from bottom left to top right) determines to which new "
"brightness level (on the vertical axis) pixels with a certain original level "
"(on the horizontal axis) are to be mapped. For example, the default diagonal "
"line from bottom left to top right sets every original pixel to its own "
"brightness value, meaning no change. A horizontal line means that all pixels "
"will get the same brightness. This means minimal contrast, the brightness "
"itself is indicated by the height at which the line is placed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click on a handle (red circle) to select it (a selected handle is "
"indicated by a filled circle) and drag it around to change the shape of the "
"curve. The curve will be drawn smoothly through the handles (always strictly "
"from left to right). If you click on the curve, a handle is added to it at "
"that position. Clicking somewhere else in the image will also add a handle "
"at that point. You can press <keycap>Delete</keycap> to delete the currently "
"selected handle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Bumpmap</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Bumpmap</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Bumpmap</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Bumpmap</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can apply a bumpmap effect and customize it using this dialog. One layer "
"is used as bumpmap layer: it is read as grayscale image and the gray values "
"of its pixels are used to to distort the other layer for creating the depth "
"illusion. High grey values, &ie; more white, mean a larger height, small "
"values, &ie; near black, mean a smaller height &mdash; or a larger depth, "
"the height can get <quote>below sealevel</quote>. A light source, shining "
"<quote>from above</quote> on the image that lies <quote>on the ground</"
"quote>, is simulated to determine the depth and direction of the shadows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first option in this dialog offers you the selection of the "
"<guilabel>Bumpmap layer</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Type</guilabel>, you can select what kind of bumpmap to be "
"applied. There are three types, <guilabel>Linear</guilabel> (a normal "
"application of the bumpmap), <guilabel>Spherical</guilabel> (focusing on the "
"extremes, that is, the shadow and highlight values) and "
"<guilabel>Sinusoidal</guilabel> (focusing on the midtone values)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then, there are three options to modify the bumpmap apart from its "
"algorithmical application. With <guilabel>Compensate for darkening</"
"guilabel>, the image is restored to about its original average lightness if "
"using the bumpmap filter would make it darker. The <guilabel>Invert bumpmap</"
"guilabel> option creates an inverted bumpmap (high and low are reversed). "
"With <guilabel>Tile bumpmap</guilabel>, a bumpmap layer that is smaller than "
"the layer it is applied to, will be tiled (repeatedly) to cover the entire "
"layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Settings</guilabel>, you can select the mathematical "
"parameters for the bumpmap. First of all, <guilabel>Azimuth</guilabel> (the "
"angle of the light source in the X-Y plane), <guilabel>Elevation</guilabel> "
"(the height of the simulated light source above the surface in degrees, with "
"0 degrees being on the ground and 90 degrees being vertically above the "
"image), and <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> (the maximal vertical distortion of "
"the image)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then, there are the <guilabel>X offset</guilabel> and <guilabel>Y offset</"
"guilabel>, with which you can displace the bumpmap layer relative to the "
"destination layer, <guilabel>Water level</guilabel> (the depth seen as "
"neutral), and <guilabel>Ambient light</guilabel>, which determines the "
"relative amount of ambient (environmental) light."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Color Adjustment</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Color Adjustment</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Color Adjustment</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:754
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Color Adjustment</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog allows you to customize the <guilabel>Color Adjustment</"
"guilabel> filter. You can use the curve (see the section on <link linkend="
"\"commands-dialogs-filters-brightnesscontrast\">Brightness / Contrast</link> "
"for a description on the curve) to determine the mapping from old to new "
"color levels, for each of the channels separately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Color to Alpha</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Color to Alpha</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Color to Alpha</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Color to Alpha</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:787
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can make parts of the image having a certain color "
"transparent (officially <quote>alpha-transparent</quote>). You can select "
"the color you want to remove from the image (replacing it with transparency) "
"with the <guilabel>Color</guilabel> swatch, and how much a color may differ "
"from the selected one before it is considered not to match, with the "
"<guilabel>Threshold</guilabel> spinbox. Setting a threshold of zero (0) "
"ensures that only pixels with the exact matching color will be made "
"transparent, higher thresholds will make other colors match as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Color Transfer</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:804
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Color Transfer</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Color Transfer</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:812
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Color Transfer</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:817
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog lets you copy the colors from one image (the <guilabel>Reference "
"Image</guilabel>) to the current one. The colors in both images are compared "
"and each color in the one you are working with, will be replaced by the "
"nearest one in the reference image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Custom Convolution</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:860
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Custom Convolution</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:866
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Custom Convolution</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:868
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Custom Convolution</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:873
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this filter, you can apply a customized distortion effect to your "
"image. The nine spinboxes at the top left determine the distortion. Each "
"pixel is assigned a new value based on these values: the old color values of "
"the pixel inself and the eight surrounding pixels are each multiplied by the "
"values in the respective spinboxes, these results are added, and the final "
"result is the new color value for the pixel. Before being applied, this "
"final result can be multiplied with a certain <guilabel>Factor</guilabel> or "
"a certain <guilabel>Offset</guilabel> can be added to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the example screenshot, each pixel is assigned a new value based on its "
"own (the 1 in the center), to which are added the values of the pixels to "
"its top right and directly below it (each with a factor of 1, &ie; the "
"actual value, since multiplying by one has no effect), and from which are "
"subtracted the values of the pixels to its bottom right and directly above "
"it (added with a factor of -1, so subtracted by a factor of 1)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Emboss</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Emboss</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:904
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Emboss</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:906
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Emboss</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog contains just one option, the <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> slider "
"and spinbox which determines the depth of the embossing effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Filters Gallery</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Filters Gallery</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:929
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Filters Gallery</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Filters Gallery</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog can be used to get a quick overview of what the various "
"available filters do. The filters are in turn applied to the current image "
"and the results are put in the left list box as thumbnails. If you select "
"one, its options become available in the <guilabel>Configuration</guilabel> "
"section. See the description of the respective filter for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Gaussian Noise Reduction</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Gaussian Noise Reduction</guilabel> dialog</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Gaussian Noise Reduction</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:959
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Gaussian Noise Reduction</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:964
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog allows you to customize a Gaussian noise reduction. The "
"<guilabel>Threshold</guilabel> setting is a measure for how much noise "
"should be removed (&ie; how quickly a <quote>lonely</quote> pixel should be "
"made equal to its surroundings), while the <guilabel>Window Size</guilabel> "
"setting determines the radius of the area considered when changing pixels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Lens Correction</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:979
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Lens Correction</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Lens Correction</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:987
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Lens Correction</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:992
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can fix an image which is distorted due to common lens "
"anomalies. You can specify a <guilabel>Distortion correction</guilabel>, "
"indicating how much the image should be corrected if its concaveness / "
"convexness is not right, for areas near the center and areas near the edges. "
"If you want an asymmetrical correction, you can specify different "
"<guilabel>X</guilabel> and <guilabel>Y</guilabel> coordinates for the center "
"(in percentages of the total width and height, measured from the top left)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also correct a too light or too dark image with the "
"<guilabel>Brightness correction</guilabel> spinbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1009
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Image Restoration</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1013
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Image Restoration</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Image Restoration</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1021
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Image Restoration</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1026
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this dialog, you can specify exactly how the image restoration should "
"be done. This filter tries to increase the quality of an image, for instance "
"by removing scratches. Various options are available to customize its "
"behaviour."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1031
#, no-c-format
msgid "(Unfortunately, these are not described as of yet.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1038
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Oilpaint</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1042
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Oilpaint</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Oilpaint</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1050
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Oilpaint</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1055
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog can configure two parameters for the associated filter. The "
"<guilabel>Brush size</guilabel> setting determines the size of the brush "
"that is used to simulate the oilpaint effect, the <guilabel>Smooth</"
"guilabel> setting specifies if the difference in colors between adjacent "
"<quote>swatches</quote> may be large (low smoothness) or should be small "
"(high smoothness)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Pixelize</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1071
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Pixelize</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1077
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Pixelize</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1079
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Pixelize</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this dialog, you can adjust two settings. <guilabel>Pixel width</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Pixel height</guilabel> indicate the width and "
"height of the area that should be taken together and averaged to form one "
"new, large <quote>pixel</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1094
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Raindrops</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1098
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Raindrops</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Raindrops</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1106
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Raindrops</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This filter can be configured using the settings <guilabel>Drop size</"
"guilabel> (the average diameter of the raindrops), <guilabel>Number</"
"guilabel> (the number of raindrop effects that should be added to the "
"image), and <guilabel>Fish eyes</guilabel> (the percentage of raindrops that "
"should be rendered as fisheye lens effects instead of plain raindrop "
"effects)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1122
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Random Noise</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1126
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Random Noise</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1132
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Random Noise</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Random Noise</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This filter adds random noise (speckles, or something similar) to your "
"image. There are two customizable settings: the amount of noise "
"(<guilabel>Level</guilabel>, as a percentage) and the <guilabel>Opacity</"
"guilabel> of the noise (should the original color still be a bit visible or "
"not)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1149
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Random Pick</guilabel> dialog</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1153
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Random Pick</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1159
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Random Pick</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1161
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Random Pick</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-dialogs.docbook:1166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog, you can specify parameters for the <guilabel>Random Pick</"
"guilabel> filter. The <guilabel>Level</guilabel> setting determines how much "
"pixels will be affected (measured as a percentage), the area which is looked "
"in to take a new color for a pixel is set with the <guilabel>Size of the "
"window</guilabel> setting, and the <guilabel>Opacity</guilabel> of the "
"modifications can be set as well."
msgstr ""

